# Site settings for the Pegasus AI Studio app.
# Install on the PORTAL host as /etc/ood/config/apps/bc_pegasus_ai_studio/site.env
# template/script.sh.erb bakes it into each session's job script when the
# dashboard renders it, so compute nodes need no copy. Plain shell; $HOME
# expands on the session host to the user's real home.

# --- Where workflows run ("compute") ---
# A Pegasus site catalog for this cluster, e.g. site "compute" sent to Slurm
# through HTCondor BLAHP (see README "Workflows on Slurm"). It replaces
# Studio's own default catalog for every user; it must be readable inside the
# session, so keep it on a path the app binds (the image directory, say).
#STUDIO_SITE_CATALOG_FILE=/opt/pegasus-ai/studio/site-catalog.yml
#STUDIO_SITE_CATALOG_LABEL="Unity (Slurm)"
# ...or the name of a catalog published in pegasushub/pegasus-site-catalogs:
#STUDIO_SITE_CATALOG=unity.yml

# --- AI assistant ---
# An OpenAI-compatible gateway the site runs. Leave unset and users add their
# own provider and API key in Settings. Never put a key here: every user could
# read it from their own session.
#STUDIO_LLM_GATEWAY_URL=https://llm.example.edu/v1
#STUDIO_LLM_DEFAULT_MODEL=default

# --- HTCondor access point ---
# When sessions do not run on the access point. Fully qualified names only:
# HTCondor rejects a bare host name ("unknown host").
#_CONDOR_SCHEDD_HOST=ap.example.edu
#_CONDOR_COLLECTOR_HOST=cm.example.edu
